&HEAD CHID='particle_contact_cooling', TITLE='Solid particles resting on a floor of fixed temperature: contact conduction only' /

Four steel particles rest on the floor, each in its own floor cell. Radiation and convection are off, so heat moves only
by contact conduction, Q = h_s A_c (T_w - T_s), where A_c is the particle footprint (projected area). For a particle of
uniform conductivity this is a convective-type boundary condition with h = h_s A_c / A over the whole particle surface
(sphere h_s/4, cylinder lying flat h_s/pi, plate h_s/2). The exact surface temperature is the series solution for transient
conduction in a sphere, a long cylinder and a plate (Incropera et al., Fundamentals of Heat and Mass Transfer, Sec. 5.6).
Sphere, cylinder and plate start at 900 C on a 20 C floor. A fourth sphere starts at 20 C on a patch of floor held at 600 C.

&MESH IJK=12,4,4, XB=0.0,0.6,0.0,0.2,0.0,0.2 /
&TIME T_END=200., DT=0.05 /
&MISC NOISE=F /
&RADI RADIATION=.FALSE. /

&SURF ID='COLD FLOOR', TMP_FRONT=20., TAU_T=0., HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT=0., COLOR='GRAY' /
&SURF ID='HOT FLOOR',  TMP_FRONT=600., TAU_T=0., HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT=0., COLOR='RED' /
&VENT XB=0.50,0.55,0.10,0.15,0.0,0.0, SURF_ID='HOT FLOOR' /
&VENT MB='ZMIN', SURF_ID='COLD FLOOR' /

&MATL ID='STEEL', DENSITY=7850., CONDUCTIVITY=45., SPECIFIC_HEAT=0.46 /

&SURF ID='SPHERE',      MATL_ID='STEEL', THICKNESS=0.005,  GEOMETRY='SPHERICAL',   TMP_INNER=900., HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT=0. /
&SURF ID='CYLINDER',    MATL_ID='STEEL', THICKNESS=0.0032, LENGTH=0.038, GEOMETRY='CYLINDRICAL', TMP_INNER=900., HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT=0. /
&SURF ID='PLATE',       MATL_ID='STEEL', THICKNESS=0.003,  LENGTH=0.02, WIDTH=0.02, GEOMETRY='CARTESIAN', TMP_INNER=900., HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT=0. /
&SURF ID='COLD SPHERE', MATL_ID='STEEL', THICKNESS=0.005,  GEOMETRY='SPHERICAL',   TMP_INNER=20.,  HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT=0. /

&PART ID='sphere',      SURF_ID='SPHERE',      HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT_SOLID=500., SAMPLING_FACTOR=1 /
&PART ID='cylinder',    SURF_ID='CYLINDER',    HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT_SOLID=500., SAMPLING_FACTOR=1, DRAG_LAW='CYLINDER' /
&PART ID='plate',       SURF_ID='PLATE',       HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT_SOLID=500., SAMPLING_FACTOR=1 /
&PART ID='cold sphere', SURF_ID='COLD SPHERE', HEAT_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENT_SOLID=500., SAMPLING_FACTOR=1 /

&INIT ID='sphere',      PART_ID='sphere',      XYZ=0.075,0.125,0.004, N_PARTICLES=1 /
&INIT ID='cylinder',    PART_ID='cylinder',    XYZ=0.225,0.125,0.004, N_PARTICLES=1 /
&INIT ID='plate',       PART_ID='plate',       XYZ=0.375,0.125,0.004, N_PARTICLES=1 /
&INIT ID='cold sphere', PART_ID='cold sphere', XYZ=0.525,0.125,0.004, N_PARTICLES=1 /

&DEVC ID='T_sphere',      QUANTITY='WALL TEMPERATURE', INIT_ID='sphere',      TIME_AVERAGED=.FALSE. /
&DEVC ID='T_cylinder',    QUANTITY='WALL TEMPERATURE', INIT_ID='cylinder',    TIME_AVERAGED=.FALSE. /
&DEVC ID='T_plate',       QUANTITY='WALL TEMPERATURE', INIT_ID='plate',       TIME_AVERAGED=.FALSE. /
&DEVC ID='T_cold_sphere', QUANTITY='WALL TEMPERATURE', INIT_ID='cold sphere', TIME_AVERAGED=.FALSE. /

&TAIL /
